  "question": {
    "text": "An electron, a doubly ionized helium ion ($He^{++}$) and proton are having the same kinetic energy. The relation between their respective de-Broglie wavelength&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>*</mo></msup></msub><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><msup><mi>He</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></msub></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub></math> is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\lambda_e>\\lambda_{{He}^{++}}>\\lambda_p$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\lambda_e<\\lambda_{{He}^{++}}==\\lambda_p$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\lambda_e>\\lambda_p>\\lambda_{{He}^{++}}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\lambda_e<\\lambda_p<\\lambda_{{He}^{++}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\lambda=\\frac{h}{m v}=\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{2 m k}}$<br>$\\lambda_{\\mathrm{e}}: \\lambda_{\\mathrm{p}}: \\lambda_{{He}^{++}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{e}}}}: \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{p}}}}: \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\mathrm{He}^{++}}}$<br>$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9.1 \\times 10^{-31}}}: \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1.6 \\times 10^{-27}}}: \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4 \\times 1.6 \\times 10^{-27}}}=84: 2: 1$"
  }
